  "goodToKnow": "Die Grafschaft is a county, historically land ruled by a Graf (count). Germany's modern districts are Landkreise, but some regions keep historic names, like die Grafschaft Bentheim, and English counties are called Grafschaften. Der Graf (die Gräfin) is a count or countess. Graf Zeppelin, inventor of the airship, and the conspirator Graf von Stauffenberg (20 July 1944) are famous Grafen. Plural: die Grafschaften."
